//! Files in the project, read when called — bind them at the top level, not in
//! `draw`. Paths are `Path.t` values — relative to the entry file's folder and
//! inside the project (see `Path`); a bare string is a check error. Desktop,
//! `functor export`, and Quest (`functor run vr` pushes the project's files
//! first); not the web yet.
//!
//! Data you don't ship (game files the player owns) goes under an external
//! prefix, declared in `config`: `Config.external("ss2/", Source.mount("ss2"))`.
//! Each machine maps the mount, never the code: `~/.config/functor/mounts.json`
//! holds `{"ss2": "~/ss2/sshock2.kpf!data/res/"}` (a folder, or `!` into a
//! zip), or pass `--mount ss2=PATH`. Then
//! `File.bytes(Path.of("ss2/mesh/x.bin"))` reads `data/res/mesh/x.bin` in the
//! archive, case-sensitively in a zip (a folder follows its disk;
//! `Source.ignoreCase` for data that names files in any case). External folders are never pushed or bundled. On Quest, `functor run vr` sends them when the game
//! first asks: `File.exists` is false until then, and the game reloads once
//! they arrive.

/// The bytes of a file: `"data/model.bin" |> Path.of |> File.bytes`.
impure[file]
let bytes : (Path.t) => Bytes.t
/// Whether the project has the file — e.g. to fall back when an optional,
/// uncommitted input (a game asset) isn't there.
impure[file]
let exists : (Path.t) => bool
